<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martin Luther</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1483–1546</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin Luther was a German theologian and monk whose Ninety-five Theses of 1517 began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation</a>. Born at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisleben">Eisleben</a> in the County of Mansfeld, he refused to recant before Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-worms">Diet of Worms</a> in 1521. Protected by Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-of-saxony">Frederick the Wise</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, he translated the Bible into German, and his teachings became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-luther.jpg" alt="Martin Luther" width="320" height="506" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Martin_Luther,_1528_(Veste_Coburg).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
